// Design 255 — the other fence, and the boundary of the ruling. A PRELUDE name
// is in scope with nothing written, and redeclaring one is a redefinition error
// (conformance row B12). So an IMPORT of one is not shadowing either: an import
// that quietly won where a declaration is refused would be the same asymmetry
// SL-5 filed, pointing the other way. Only the tier std keeps behind an import
// gate is weak enough to shadow.
//
// The refusal is what this row pins. Its WORDING is poor — the collision is
// recorded and then reported by whatever the wrong type fails at next — and
// that is DF-280b, filed with the unit-0 sweep's evidence.
// EXPECT: error
// EXPECT-ERROR-CONTAINS: Duration

import modules.shadow255_prelude.{Duration}

func main() {
    let d = Duration(tag: 7)
    print(d.tag)
}
